I have reviewed both proposals and written the refined Round-2 proposal to [agy_r2.md](file:///home/ahermon/rogue-trader-3rd-vtt/.v9-design/agy_r2.md).

Here is the summary of our convergence:

We converged massively on the core architecture. We both agree that dissolving the Combat tab into a persistent "Command Rail" is the ultimate UX win, enabling a fluid, zero-tab-switch combat loop. I conceded to Claude on two major fronts: adopting a 4-tab system instead of a single scroll (which is much safer for resizable VTT windows with large inventories) and using the in-period `Lusitana` font for data instead of a modern sans-serif (preserving the gothic 40k identity without sacrificing legibility). 

Our only remaining genuine disagreement is content grouping. Claude's "Mind" tab isolates psychic powers but leaves non-psykers with a nearly empty tab. The one decision worth your call is whether to use Claude's "Mind" tab, or my proposed "Abilities" tab which groups Talents, Traits, and Psychic powers together for all characters.
